WEBVTT

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.530
Winter. February.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.000
They began as if they were waiting...

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.640
for the SV2's Second Unit to go on vacation.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.720
In the blink of an eye, the heart of Tokyo...

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.350
was occupied by JSDF units which were roused to action.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.420
The mastermind's name was Kiyoteru Kai.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.100
Goto began at once to act in response.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.470
The members of his unit, who had left for home...

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.270
hurriedly made their way back to Tokyo.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.810
But...

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.210
Morning found Tokyo wrapped in a blanket of snow...

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.370
which had fallen in the night.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:13.080
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:19.560
HAATO BIITO wo awaserya sore de ikisou yo
If I can get my heartbeat under control, I think I'll make it

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:25.270
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:30.910
takaku hayaku suki yo ki mama ni
Higher, faster, I'll love you if I want to

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:37.460
METARU BODII no hadazawari sae
I think I'll get to like

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:43.400
atsuku kanjite kuru kuse ni narisou
The way I get flushed at the touch of your metal body

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:49.690
CHACHI na Imagination koeta jigen de
Oh, don't stop this gravity-defying feeling

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:56.580
juuryokuihan ah nukeru Feeling tomenai de
That goes way beyond mere imagination

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:03.100
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.550
PITAri kakarerya PIKAA kireru ARUFONSU
When I hold him tight, my Alphonse can do anything

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:15.180
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:23.760
sora mo umi mo kyou mo ashita mo Nothin' impossible
Anytime, anywhere, nothing's impossible

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.720
Nothing's impossible

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:38.050
The SV2's Longest Day
Part 2

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:43.680
We repeat, early this morning, the area bounded by Hanzoumon...

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:48.820
Miyakezaka, Sakuradamon, Toranomon, and Akasakamitsuke...

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.900
have been occupied by members of the JSDF.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.800
The Defense Agency has denied any involvement in these actions.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.400
The forces responsible have been declared rebels...

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.070
but currently, five hours after the incident began...

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:08.380
those units have issued no statements or demands whatsoever...

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.810
so this incident is still shrouded in mystery.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.680
At this time, all regular programming has been cancelled so that...

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:15.950
- Thanks.
- Come again!

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.600
Hello, Shanghai Restaurant here.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.500
This is Mikiyama over on 2nd. Is my ramen ready yet?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.090
Is that you, Shinshi? What happened?

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.430
Just like you said, Captain. The JSDF has occupied the SV2 building.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.940
Gimme some <i>natto</i>!

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.910
Right. And Kanuka just went there to check things over.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.610
I can't believe the restaurant is helping you out.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.450
Our people practically own the place.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.450
They'd help us, no matter what we needed.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.920
So what about the Labors? Is there anything we can do?

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.880
No. Unit 2 is in pieces, and we've cannibalized so many parts from...

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.020
our spare, Unit 3, that it's just a shell.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.000
And anyway, they've taken the startup disks.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.860
It's frustrating, but we can't use any of our Labors.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.200
So we have to rely on the one you sent out to Hachiouji, then.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.930
Hey! What's taking so long in there?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.640
Cut me some slack! These guys just gave me a 10,000-yen bill!

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.240
I can't make change for that so early in the morning!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.480
Think you could spot me? I'll knock 1,050 yen off your bill.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.150
Just hurry it up!

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.820
Hold on.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:28.090
There's one on display over at the Nakano Police Academy.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.460
But that thing's...

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.330
It'll run. I did its last maintenance check <i>myself!</i> It'll run!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.340
- Okay, Nakano it is.
- Hey, hold on.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.340
Actually, there's something that's been worrying me.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.040
What?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.580
Shige said that he wasn't sure, but <i>still</i>.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.550
- How did you sneak these out?
- Right.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.050
He heard one of them say, "We've got a nuke."

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.320
I hear there's a civil war going on in Tokyo!

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.200
No more flights are going in the afternoon? I wonder what's gonna happen?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.240
We will soon begin our landing. Please fasten your seatbelt...

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.840
and return your seat to its fully upright position.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.250
Our landing time will be 11:15.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:28.380
The weather at Haneda is clear at 45 degrees.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:33.390
The state of emergency caused by rebel units is still in progress...

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.860
so please be aware that the Loop Line...

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.090
and subway lines within the Loop are stopped.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.810
SV2 First Unit commander, Asst. Inspector Shinobu Nagumo, reporting.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:58.910
Good. I'm speaking with you from the Fuchuu PD via cable.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:03.210
Most key government officials, from the Cabinet members on down...

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:06.990
were apparently taken by surprise and have been detained.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.190
Sobue and I, who happened to be out of town on business...

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.890
have set up a temporary command post here.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.700
Until the situation shows signs of clearing up...

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.400
I will command all of the city's police departments from here.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.510
With things the way they are, I can't issue written orders...

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.410
so I hereby appoint you garrison commander.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.350
Relay these orders immediately:

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:33.080
Order the garrison to break through the siege...

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:37.350
and once clear, to withdraw immediately and regroup here.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.620
You can't be serious. You want us to <i>hand</i> over the area...

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.590
and run away with our tail between our legs?

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.690
Watch your tongue!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.860
Orders to defend to the death I could understand...

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.730
but why are you ordering us to withdraw without engaging the enemy?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:56.470
We recently received a message through the U.S. ambassador.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:00.140
An aerial-launch cruise missile that had been secretly...

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:05.010
brought into the U.S. air base at Yokota has been stolen.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.980
This happened two days ago.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:11.390
They had planned to bring it back with them when LIMPAC ended.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.090
I can't believe they brought that into the country!

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.600
That won't get us anywhere!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.320
The rebels, which you would think...

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.660
would be hoping for a short-term civil war...

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.170
still haven't issued so much as a single statement.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:26.070
This may mean that they are either playing at having reserves...

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.400
or it may be a sign of certainty that they have a trump card.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.840
In any case, given the situation, it's safe to assume...

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.010
that they have a nuclear missile in their possession.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.080
I assume you understand that if you clash with their siege units...

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.420
police units who are facing off against the rebels...

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.490
will automatically begin to fight them throughout the city.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.620
JSDF commanders who were watching from the sideline will step in...

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.170
and we will find ourselves in the middle of an all-out civil war.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:57.000
If that happens, they'll announce their trump card.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.130
All of Japan will fall into a panic.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.370
What we must do now is buy time and find a way to resolve this.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.180
If that's understood, return to your post and relay my orders.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.450
But you must keep secret that we spoke to you from this location.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.780
Dismissed.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:17.720
Why are you standing there? Carry out your orders!

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.150
- I can't.
- Nagumo!

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.630
I can't agree to this.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.050
The area around and above the siege line is packed with reporters.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.620
The eyes of the country are on us, wondering what's going on.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.200
If we just hand over HQ without firing a single shot...

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.600
without any sort of resistance whatsoever...

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:37.140
it will be as if the police have acknowledged their defeat!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.140
Isn't that exactly what they want us to do?

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.010
<i>We</i> are the ones who are to protect the country...

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.610
against those who would take it over.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:49.820
The hopes of the country are riding on us.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.360
To give in to their bluff without any solid evidence... no, even...

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:57.690
if there <i>were</i> such evidence... without a fight is inexcusable!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:03.000
Even if every garrison member dies here, we mustn't move an inch!

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.330
This decision was made at the highest political levels.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.700
It's not your place to question the motives of your superiors!

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:11.370
I'm told that you were waiting there since last night.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.640
How, exactly, did you predict what would happen today?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.710
It was Captain Goto.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.810
Goto's whereabouts are still unknown.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.980
We can only conclude that he has deliberately cut communications.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:27.720
Are you aware, Nagumo, that when Goto was a college student...

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.790
he and Kai, the rebel leader, were friends?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.390
What are you two up to?

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.990
Or to be more precise, are you working with Goto...

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:40.300
conspiring with the rebels, inciting the garrison...

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.810
and trying to use this situation to your own advantage?

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:48.550
Well, it seems you've shown your true colors.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.580
Assistant Inspector Nagumo, I hereby strip you of your rank...

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:56.250
and place you under arrest on suspicion of rebel conspiracy.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:01.750
You blind fools.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.400
- Come with me.
- Keep your hands off me!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:11.530
I will hereby act independently.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.370
If you feel it necessary, feel free to punish me.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.100
<i>But</i> if you intend to stand in my way, bear in mind...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.610
that I will disclose the contents of this conversation.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.280
- Restrain her!
- Yes, sir!

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.660
Two days ago? That's the same time as that checkpoint break.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.600
I get it now. Even if they cut loose with a machine gun...

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.060
they'd get away clean.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:44.130
I have to admit, I'm surprised! That's clear-cut insubordination.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:46.740
You should have run away, like I said.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.270
What are you talking about?

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.280
Um, it's nothing. I was just talking to myself.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:55.210
But even if this mess is cleared up, those people won't...

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.870
get away unscathed once they start doling out responsibility.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:02.220
The way things are going, that's what's going to happen.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:05.550
And <i>you've</i> got room to talk! <i>You</i> dragged me into this!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.320
You're a criminal, too! I bet the police are after you!

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:13.230
I'm awfully busy as it is. I don't know if I can deal with the police.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.770
Anyway, thanks for the information.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.770
Where <i>are</i> you, anyway? What are you planning?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.570
And what's your connection to this "Kai" man?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.870
I don't think the siege units will do anything...

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.950
so don't try anything crazy.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.910
- I'll call you later.
- Hey!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.090
Nakano Police Academy

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.680
Come back here!

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.620
Ota! This way!

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:40.850
Hurry!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.030
This is an awful lot like robbery, Ota.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.860
We'll get into trouble later!

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.630
Moron! That was a judgement call!

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.370
That damned commandant just <i>had</i> to open his mouth!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:58.880
Aren't you going to Sakuradamon, Kanuka?

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.470
What do you think we can do with this pile of scrap?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.950
Just leave everything to me.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.180
Oh, we're gonna raise some hell!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.450
Yeah, whatever! Could you try driving right?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.320
This stupid seat is rotted through! My ass hurts!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:18.400
A truck with a Labor on it is going down the wrong side of the road!

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.100
Can I go, Officer?

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.170
Yeah, go.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.800
Thanks.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.010
Shanghai Restaurant here.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:37.010
Hey, Shinohara! Glad you could make it. Is Izumi with you?

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.650
Ota and the rest? They're fine.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.380
They're driving the wrong way down the Koushuu Highway...

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.550
and are drawing a lot of cops after them.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.350
I have <i>no</i> idea what they're doing.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:50.030
<i>What</i>? You saw Kai in Tomakomai?

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.730
It was yesterday morning at a noodle shop at the station.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:59.030
Right, he ordered it without onions and then heaped on cayenne pepper.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.430
How did you know that?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.810
Yes, sir! Yes, sir! Understood!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:04.810
Did you hear that?

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.000
Not a word.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.670
Alphonse is okay!

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:11.310
He's at Hachiouji, so he said to go there and wait for further orders!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.250
Awesome! Yes! Yes! <i>Yes</i>!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.080
Hey! Cut it out!

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.850
If his trump card is to attack a city with that cruise missile...

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.620
then his target is Tokyo.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.920
And rather than attempt a high-risk aerial launch...

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:30.900
he'll opt for a guerilla action using a simple launcher.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.270
In any case, Hokkaido is too far away.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.640
He was seen in Tomakomai.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.870
That trailer fled away from Sendai.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.040
What's the connection?

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:46.250
Tomakomai... Sendai... Tomakomai... Sendai...

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.280
Tomakomai...

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.720
Tomakomai             Sendai                Tokyo
Japan Coastal Ferries

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.530
We can't wait around any longer.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.430
Looks like your boss is hard to get a hold of.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.530
All the police in Japan are a little busy.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.300
I'm out of here. Thanks for the information on the missile.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:10.230
I told you because you're a fellow American.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.710
Remember to keep your source confidential, okay?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.750
A court-martial isn't my idea of fun.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.810
You know, I think I may be entitled to a little hush money.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:30.160
She calls <i>this</i> "hush money"?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.860
You know, I've been thinking.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:37.340
Maybe Kanuka was <i>exiled</i> here under the pretext of research.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:41.740
Maybe <i>they</i> couldn't keep her under control, either.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.710
What? You can't find the driver?

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.620
No. I've looked inside and around the car.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.020
But look at how far this thing fell! He couldn't have...

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.290
What's with you?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:04.420
Well, uh... my ambulance is gone.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.360
Hello, Johtoh Bureau? My name's Goto.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.500
Is Inspector Matsui there? He's in Investigations Dept. 1.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:14.930
Goto?

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:19.140
Stop screwing around! Go and get me some information!

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.540
What the hell did you do?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.670
There's a wanted notice for you even out <i>here</i>!

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:26.120
It says to arrest you on sight!

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:29.020
I got saddled with a short-tempered partner.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:32.580
Anyway, you have some pull over at Maritime Safety, right?

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:34.560
I guess.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.990
Could you do me a favor?

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.220
We saved your hide during that sea monster ruckus, remember?

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.430
At a time like <i>this</i>?

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.530
I'm asking <i>because</i> it's a time like this.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.500
I'll be waiting for you there.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:50.570
Hello, my name is Kubo.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:54.110
Yes, there <i>is</i> a ferry going from Tomakomai to Tokyo via Sendai...

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:58.510
that veered off course after we lost contact with it last night.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:15:59.950
- That's it!
- Excuse me?

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:01.320
Nevermind. And?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:04.320
With what's going on and all, we thought it was possible...

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.860
that it had been sea-jacked by the rebels.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:10.160
Our superiors felt the same way, so we sent out a chopper.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.630
Um, this <i>is</i> confidential, all right?

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:16.170
This is the <i>Safflower</i>, registered to Japan Coastal Ferries.

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:19.330
It's cruising about 20km off of Choushi.

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:25.600
What do you see here?

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:29.510
A torpedo launcher? No, that can't be it.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:33.250
That's not what it is, but you're not far off.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:34.680
And then there's this.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.280
You have more?

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.950
Yes. There's one other ship.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.730
The <i>Pacific</i>, registered to Pacific Ferries.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.760
It's moving south, parallel to the <i>Safflower</i>, about 2km east of it.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.520
There's one here, too!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.560
What the heck <i>are</i> those?

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:55.710
One is probably a pipe or something like that, made up as a dummy.

00:16:55.810 --> 00:17:01.540
The other one is a cruise missile that has a range of 150km.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:15.510
Safflower

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:21.390
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.390
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.340
There's a call for you, Commander.

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:49.710
- For <i>me</i>?
- Yes, sir. He says his name is Goto.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.450
I knew you'd show up.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:55.520
You sound well.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:59.080
Like they say, "Ill weeds are sure to thrive."

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:02.280
Anyway, since you're calling me here, I assume you've seen it.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.950
Did it show up all right in the pictures?

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.360
Yeah. Looks like you've got yourself a nasty toy.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.830
Of course, there's no proof that it's the real thing, though.

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:14.800
If I use it, you'll find out, like it or not.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.530
No, thanks.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:19.310
Look, Goto, you don't stand a chance.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.640
It's not too late. Why not join me?

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.750
Again, no, thanks.

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:27.580
I doubt you've forgotten that that's why I became a cop.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:28.980
That's too bad.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:31.920
I sent out an ultimatum five minutes ago.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:37.360
If any ships or aircraft come within 1 km of either of my ships...

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.290
I will see it as an act of hostility...

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.630
and will immediately launch the missile.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.770
The same thing will happen if I don't receive a favorable answer...

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.100
from the government before the deadline. That is all.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:05.580
Captain! Where have you been?

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:08.420
Kanuka left a message for you. Let's see here.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:11.500
"The missile that was stolen from Yokota was an M-69 SLAM...

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:14.530
a short-range cruise missile designed to be mounted in a B-1.

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.730
Launched from the air, its range is 150km.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.030
When using terrain-matching guidance, it's 60km.

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.870
It's armed with a nuclear warhead."

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:25.100
Oh, and Hiromi landed at Haneda. He's waiting for instructions.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:28.400
So what the heck are we going to do? We're...

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:33.150
I'm Jitsuyama, the factory manager here.

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.810
The company president has authorized me...

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:39.450
to donate a paratrooper Labor that we're currently developing...

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:44.020
That greedy bastard just wants to show it off to boost sales later!

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:49.000
Anyway, what good's a paratrooper gonna be against a nuclear missile?

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:52.500
Huh? You can use it? You're at Yokosuka?

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:56.730
Yes, sir! Officers Shinohara and Izumi will depart immediately!

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:58.770
Kanuka and the rest, sir?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.710
They're storming Sakuradamon, apparently.

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.440
They said something about raising some hell.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:09.680
I repeat, if you continue to flee, you will be attacked!

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:10.910
Stop your vehicles at once!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.750
I'm gonna shoot him! I can shoot him, can't I?

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:15.420
Taking on a moving target will just eat up your ammo!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.860
At this range, he can't use his missiles or his mini-gun!

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:21.260
He's circling around to get into position!

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:22.990
Next time, he'll mean business!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:32.870
Prepare to fire!

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:37.110
You always lie in wait for somebody at the mouth of a tunnel!

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:49.760
Shinshi!

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:53.960
Keep us steady! You know what I'll do if you try a U-turn!

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.220
R-Roger!

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:28.990
Idiots.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.160
R-Retreat! Retreat!

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:52.150
I'm surprised you got permission from the Americans to do this.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:55.380
They'll catch hell if this is made public, same as us.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.980
People with a weak spot all tend to be cooperative.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:03.930
Their public stance is that they're watching from the sideline.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.260
They agreed, but on the condition that...

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:09.930
they leave the area right after launching Yamazaki.

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:12.600
Is Hiromi okay with this?

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:15.400
He volunteered to do it.

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:18.450
Anyway, he can take the launch's G-forces better than anyone.

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:20.810
- Come on, we'd better get going.
- Yes, sir!

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:28.720
Two escorts to port. One to starboard.

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:30.560
Several high-speed recon craft.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.290
The helicopters look like reporters...

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.630
but at that range, an anti-ship missile would get here in seconds.

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:38.630
Should we pull away and open the distance a little, Commander?

00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:41.640
This is a civilian ship that doesn't have a long-range radar.

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:45.730
If they wanted to, they could sink us before we knew what hit us.

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:49.610
But they don't have the guts to kill hundreds of passengers...

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:52.580
along with us with so many witnesses around.

00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:54.910
That's why I drew them out here.

00:22:55.750 --> 00:22:58.120
Labor approaching off the starboard bow!

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:01.890
It looks like one of the SV2's Type-98 AVs!

00:23:02.890 --> 00:23:03.990
So they came.

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:10.060
It's me. Put him through.

00:23:10.770 --> 00:23:12.330
Goto? Give it up.

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:15.960
I don't know what you're thinking, but even a child would know...

00:23:16.070 --> 00:23:17.870
that something this blatant is a decoy.

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:21.040
You don't say. Then what about that missile of yours...

00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:22.980
that you've been parading around?

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:26.210
It may be human nature to keep your trump card close to you...

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:27.780
but it's damn poor strategy.

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:31.550
But you can trick your opponent by showing him that.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:34.720
That was always your forte, as I recall.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:38.420
Don't you remember? Who do you think taught me?

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:42.030
That's the way, Goto. Draw out your opponent...

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:45.070
and keep him talking and never let him see your weak spot.

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:48.430
Keep him off-balance, make him say what he shouldn't have said...

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:52.870
and he'll erode his own advantage. You were my best student, all right.

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:54.100
I have to go.

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:00.370
Here is your target: Kai is on the <i>Safflower</i>.

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:03.010
Pay no attention to the other ship.

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:05.880
I repeat, your target is the <i>Safflower</i>!

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:07.720
Unit 1, roger!

00:24:07.990 --> 00:24:10.120
The nuclear sub has signaled "roger."

00:24:10.330 --> 00:24:12.760
They'll be in position in five minutes.

00:24:13.830 --> 00:24:16.430
They're coming in. Keep a close eye on the perimeter.

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:18.330
Relay that to ship #2.

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:19.860
Where's the emergency launch button?

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:21.340
That's it over there.

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:42.480
"Even with 99% certainty, a police officer's duty is to avoid...

00:24:42.590 --> 00:24:46.590
any decisive actions if there is a significant risk to human life..."

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:48.460
is what you want to say, right?

00:24:48.570 --> 00:24:50.830
But sometimes it's too late for that.

00:24:50.930 --> 00:24:53.490
But if you're wrong...

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:57.000
If we sit around and do nothing, the outcome will be the same.

00:24:57.110 --> 00:24:58.970
Have you read his ultimatum?

00:24:59.080 --> 00:25:01.980
Dissolve the Diet. Ban political parties.

00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:04.140
Indefinitely suspend the constitution.

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:06.880
We're not talking about negotiating with a hijacker here.

00:25:06.980 --> 00:25:09.980
No government on Earth would give in to demands like that...

00:25:10.090 --> 00:25:12.060
just because they were being threatened!

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:15.390
And he's not interested in any deals, either.

00:25:15.490 --> 00:25:18.150
But what if we waited until just before the deadline?

00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:20.250
We'd lose the element of surprise.

00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:22.590
We only get one shot at this.

00:25:23.930 --> 00:25:25.600
Do you really think he'll launch it?

00:25:25.700 --> 00:25:30.640
His officers probably think it's just a bargaining tool.

00:25:30.740 --> 00:25:33.180
But he'll do it. That's the kind of man he is.

00:25:33.280 --> 00:25:35.680
And you're still going in after him?

00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:42.750
Maybe I should still arrest you after this.

00:25:46.060 --> 00:25:52.000
Goto? Are you sure you're not still on Kai's side?

00:26:05.940 --> 00:26:07.880
Sixty seconds to operation!

00:26:08.550 --> 00:26:10.210
Noa, do you read me?

00:26:10.310 --> 00:26:14.410
These things are decided in a split-second, so stay cool.

00:26:14.720 --> 00:26:16.120
I know.

00:26:17.190 --> 00:26:19.210
I'll be there soon, Hiromi.

00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:56.390
Touchdown confirmed! Let's do it!

00:26:58.260 --> 00:27:00.060
- Shoot!
- Shoot him!

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:03.530
Hiromi! The launcher! Take out the launcher!

00:27:06.470 --> 00:27:07.730
Mr. Kai!

00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:11.700
Don't do it! Mr. Kai!

00:27:36.600 --> 00:27:39.400
It's all over! Stay right where you are!

00:27:42.940 --> 00:27:44.170
Mr. Kai!

00:27:45.310 --> 00:27:47.240
It's over.

00:27:49.050 --> 00:27:51.880
It took twenty years to take what began...

00:27:51.980 --> 00:27:54.250
with two people and make it into this.

00:27:57.620 --> 00:28:00.150
But if you survive, there's always tomorrow.
